timestamp=2026-11-06T08:07:55.804Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us look further up from where the branch to Dawid Majtyka comes from\nwith open('/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\nidx = None\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'Dawid Majtyka' in line:\n        idx = i\n        break\n\n# look up more systematically\nname_pos = lines[idx].find('Dawid Majtyka') if idx else 0\n# find the closest line above that has a connector (| or branch) leading to this position\nfor j in range(idx-1, max(-1, idx-60), -1):\n    l = lines[j]\n    if name_pos < len(l) and l[name_pos] in '|+':\n        print(f'FOUND connector at line {j+1} col {name_pos}: {repr(l)}')\n        # look further up\n        break\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
