timestamp=2026-11-06T08:37:40.555Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So Dawid Majtyka appears once at (line_idx=92, col=2952)\n# Now we need to trace up to find parents, grandparents, etc. until we get to great-great-grandparent (5 generations up total?)\n# Great-great-grandparent means 4 steps up from the person: person -> parent -> grandparent -> great-grandparent -> great-great-grandparent (so 4 levels up)\n# The question says: \"Find the great-great-grandparent of 'Dawid Majtyka' in the family tree. Using the database, sum the account balances of their direct children who have more than one grandchild. Return only the final integer.\"\n# So we need: 1. Get Dawid Majtyka's great-great-grandparent GGG (i.e. parent of great-grandparent of Dawid? Or the GGG themselves). \n# That means 4 generations above Dawid: Dawid -> parent (1) -> grandparent (2) -> great-grandparent (3) -> great-great-grandparent (4). Correct.\n# Then among their DIRECT CHILDREN (i.e. children of that GGG person), find those who have MORE THAN ONE GRANDCHILD.\n# For each such child, sum their account balances from people_accounts.csv.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
