timestamp=2026-11-06T08:51:50.678Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Complicated tree. Let us look up the full lineage more systematically by tracing from Dawid step by step using the actual structure.\n# Another approach: read more about the actual layout. Maybe trace properly.\nwith open('/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# From Dawid (92,2952): parent is Juliusz Dębosz (82,2940) - we got this.\n# Now find parent of Juliusz Dębosz (82,2940)\ndef find_parent(lines, row, col):\n    for r in range(row-1, -1, -1):\n        line = lines[r]\n        import re\n        matches = re.finditer(r'\\b[A-ZĄĆĘŁŃÓŚŹŻ][a-ząćęłńóśźż]+\\s+[A-ZĄĆĘŁŃÓŚŹŻ][a-ząćęłńóśźż]+\\b', line)\n        for m in matches:\n            ncol = m.start()\n            if abs(ncol - col) < 100:\n                # check connection - look for | or + connecting\n                for rr in range(r+1, row):\n                    l2 = lines[rr]\n                    # scan wider window\n                    for dc in range(-15, 16):\n                        cc = ncol + dc\n                        if 0 <= cc < len(l2):\n                            ch = l2[cc]\n                            if ch in '|+':\n                                return (r, ncol, m.group(0))\n    return None\n\ncur = (82, 2940, 'Juliusz Dębosz')\nprint(cur)\np = find_parent(lines, cur[0], cur[1])\nprint(p)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
