timestamp=2026-11-06T09:05:51.801Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# The lineage is: Dawid Majtyka -> Juliusz Dębosz (parent) -> Kazimierz Kaziród -> Julita Kucharz -> Przemysław Kurczab -> Ewelina Rysz\n# So generations up from Dawid:\n# gen 0 (self): Dawid Majtyka\n# gen 1 (parent): Juliusz Dębosz\n# gen 2 (grandparent): Kazimierz Kaziród\n# gen 3 (great-grandparent): Julita Kucharz\n# gen 4 (great-great-grandparent): Przemysław Kurczab\n# Wait - count: parent is 1 gen up, grandparent 2, great-grandparent 3, great-great-grandparent 4. That means Przemysław Kurczab is the great-great-grandparent of Dawid.\n# Is that right? Let us confirm: Dawid's parent is Juliusz. Juliusz's parent is Kazimierz (gen2). Kazimierz's parent is Julita (gen3)? Or is Julita Kucharz Kazimierz's parent? Wait look up: in our trace, after Kazimierz Kaziród comes Julita Kucharz as parent. So Julita is Kazimierz's parent -> Julita is Dawid's great-grandparent? Because Kazimierz is grandparent (gen2), Kazimierz's parent is Julita, so Julita is great-grandparent (gen3). Then Julita's parent is Przemysław Kurczab - so Przemysław is great-great-grandparent (gen4). Correct. Then Przemysław's parent is Ewelina Rysz (gen5) - so Ewelina is 5 generations up from Dawid, i.e. Dawid's great-great-great-grandparent.\n# The question asks for \"great-great-grandparent of 'Dawid Majtyka'\". That is 4 generations up. So that is Przemysław Kurczab.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
