timestamp=2026-11-06T09:10:49.382Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Julita Kucharz has 2 children: Kazimierz Kaziród and Franciszek Grabias\n# Now for each of these children, count how many grandchildren they have.\n# Grandchildren of a child X = number of children of each of X's children (i.e. count of nodes Z such that parent of Z is Y and parent of Y is X)\n# So count total grandchildren: sum over Y in children of X of (number of children of Y)\n# Or simply count all nodes whose great-grandparent is X? Or easier: for each child Y of X, count len(children_map[Y])\n# Sum them up = total grandchildren of X through Y? Yes, each child of Y is a grandchild of X.\n\n# Also the condition is \"more than one grandchild\" (total). So if a direct child of GGG has > 1 grandchild total, then include that child's account balance in the sum.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
