timestamp=2026-11-06T09:17:05.320Z level=INFO run=694d77c8 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So in this case, direct children of GGG Przemysław: [Julita Kucharz]. \n# Does Julita Kucharz have more than one grandchild? Yes - from above, Julita has 2 grandchildren total (Kazimierz's children and Franciszek's children - but Franciszek has 0; so total grandchildren of Julita = 2). So Julita has > 1 grandchild. Therefore Julita qualifies.\n# And we sum Julita's account balance.\n# But wait - look at what we just printed: for each of Julita's children, we counted their grandchildren. That means total grandchildren of Julita = sum of grandchildren of each of her children = 2 + 0 = 2. Correct. So Julita does have > 1 grandchild.\n# That changes everything. The qualifying direct child of GGG (Przemysław) is Julita Kucharz, and we sum her balance.\n# Let us check Julita's balance.\nimport csv\n\nbalances = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/people_accounts.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        name = f\"{row['first_name']} {row['last_name']}\"\n        balances[name] = int(row['account_balance'])\n\nprint('Julita Kucharz:', balances.get('Julita Kucharz'))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
